<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<root>
  <!--
    The canonical English strings. Every other language is a Strings.<tag>.resx beside this file,
    holding only the keys it has translated - anything missing falls back through here, so an
    out-of-date translation is a partly-English app rather than a blank one.

    Keys are Page_Thing, underscored, one flat file: the key name is what a C# call site
    (Strings.Installed_Rescan) and a XAML binding ({loc:Str Installed_Rescan}) both spell, and the
    generated accessor turns a dot into an underscore anyway.

    Edit translations with ResXResourceManager's standalone build rather than by hand - it shows
    every language side by side and marks what is untranslated.
  -->
  <xsd:schema id="root" xmlns="" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:msdata="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:xml-msdata">
    <xsd:import namespace="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace" />
    <xsd:element name="root" msdata:IsDataSet="true">
      <xsd:complexType>
        <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
          <xsd:element name="metadata">
            <xsd:complexType>
              <xsd:sequence>
                <xsd:element name="value" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" />
              </xsd:sequence>
              <xsd:attribute name="name" use="required" type="xsd:string" />
              <xsd:attribute name="type" type="xsd:string" />
              <xsd:attribute name="mimetype" type="xsd:string" />
              <xsd:attribute ref="xml:space" />
            </xsd:complexType>
          </xsd:element>
          <xsd:element name="assembly">
            <xsd:complexType>
              <xsd:attribute name="alias" type="xsd:string" />
              <xsd:attribute name="name" type="xsd:string" />
            </xsd:complexType>
          </xsd:element>
          <xsd:element name="data">
            <xsd:complexType>
              <xsd:sequence>
                <xsd:element name="value" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" msdata:Ordinal="1" />
                <xsd:element name="comment" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" msdata:Ordinal="2" />
              </xsd:sequence>
              <xsd:attribute name="name" type="xsd:string" use="required" msdata:Ordinal="1" />
              <xsd:attribute name="type" type="xsd:string" msdata:Ordinal="3" />
              <xsd:attribute name="mimetype" type="xsd:string" msdata:Ordinal="4" />
              <xsd:attribute ref="xml:space" />
            </xsd:complexType>
          </xsd:element>
          <xsd:element name="resheader">
            <xsd:complexType>
              <xsd:sequence>
                <xsd:element name="value" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" msdata:Ordinal="1" />
              </xsd:sequence>
              <xsd:attribute name="name" type="xsd:string" use="required" />
            </xsd:complexType>
          </xsd:element>
        </xsd:choice>
      </xsd:complexType>
    </xsd:element>
  </xsd:schema>
  <resheader name="resmimetype">
    <value>text/microsoft-resx</value>
  </resheader>
  <resheader name="version">
    <value>2.0</value>
  </resheader>
  <resheader name="reader">
    <value>System.Resources.ResXResourceReader, System.Windows.Forms, Version=4.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b77a5c561934e089</value>
  </resheader>
  <resheader name="writer">
    <value>System.Resources.ResXResourceWriter, System.Windows.Forms, Version=4.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b77a5c561934e089</value>
  </resheader>
  <data name="Meta_LanguageName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>English</value>
    <comment>This language's name in itself, shown in the Options dropdown. A language picker names each language the way its own speakers write it, so this is the one key a translator writes in their own language rather than translating: Deutsch, not German.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Meta_ShippedLanguages" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>en</value>
    <comment>Every language tag this build ships, comma separated, English first. Adding a language means dropping in Strings.&lt;tag&gt;.resx and adding its tag here - the whole of it. Read from this file only, never from a translation, so translating this key cannot change what the app offers.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Options_Language_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Language</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Options_Language_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The language this app's own text is read in. System default follows the display language Windows is set to. Mod names, descriptions and changelogs come from the Forge and stay in whatever language their author wrote them in.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Options_Language_SystemDefaultFormat" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>System default ({0})</value>
    <comment>{0} is the language following Windows currently lands on, named in itself - "System default (English)".</comment>
  </data>
</root>
